WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.600
Why does this module matter?

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.275
The guide separates
configured from enforced.

3
00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:07.262
Configured is a setting
in an Intune policy.

4
00:00:07.262 --> 00:00:11.276
Audit mode is configured, and it
logs, but it protects nothing.

5
00:00:11.276 --> 00:00:15.088
And on Windows Server, Microsoft
lists a known issue where an Attack

6
00:00:15.088 --> 00:00:18.900
Surface Reduction rule reports
compliant without being enforced.

7
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.534
Enforced is block mode on the ring,
after the ring's exit criteria are met,

8
00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.968
proved on the device and in the events,

9
00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:29.738
with every exclusion recorded
with an owner and an expiry.

10
00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:33.032
Getting there safely is
the work of this module:

11
00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:36.663
audit first, then enforce ring
by ring, with a way back.

12
00:00:36.663 --> 00:00:41.362
The guide counts Gates 3 and 4 as the
closure map's endpoint hardening row:

13
00:00:41.362 --> 00:00:45.827
prevention baselines and Attack
Surface Reduction by staged rings,

14
00:00:45.827 --> 00:00:48.790
evidenced by policy
and endpoint telemetry.
